# Datsun Sunny B310 four-door saloon, 1978-1982.
#
# The third-generation Sunny, the last rear-wheel-drive one, sold in Britain as
# the Datsun Sunny 120Y and 140Y. The early round-headlamp car is modelled; the
# later rectangular-lamp facelift is not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Sunny
#
# Dimensions 3.940 x 1.590 x 1.365 m, wheelbase 2.340 m, from the English
# Wikipedia B310 dimension box. Production November 1977 to November 1981; UK
# sales 1978-1982.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the B310 was located, so the objects carry
# plain colour names: white, red, blue and silver. Weights white 3, red 3, blue
# 2, silver 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 145 km/h for the 1.2, the volume model; the 1.4 was quicker. Comfort
# 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: January 1978 intro, retires staggered 1994-1997 on a
# sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-sunny-b310.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-sunny-b310.dae (55 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-sunny-b310/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitation: the profile was calibrated from the published dimensions
# rather than measured from a side photograph, because none exists of a B310
# saloon on Commons. One supplied photograph was withdrawn at Gate A as a
# Toyota of the Carina/Corolla family, not a Sunny. The axle offsets and the
# intermediate body contours are therefore approximate. At 128 px the upright
# three-box body, the round lamps and the horizontal tail lamps read correctly.

obj=citycar
